  "body": "While several selection setter APIs including `setSelectionRange()` allows selection inside text controls (<input> and <textarea>), there is no straightforward way to scroll to the selected range without [hacks](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/7464282/javascript-scroll-to-selection-after-using-textarea-setselectionrange-in-chrome).\r\n\r\nGecko has a nonstandard behavior where those APIs always scroll to the internal focus offset, and I'd like to standardize this behavior:\r\n\r\n* Specify what Gecko does (always scroll to the internal focus offset)\r\n* Or, add a parameter to setSelectionRange: `setSelectionRange(start, end, { scroll: true,  direction })`\r\n* Or, add a method `scrollToFocus()`",
